-- Records a real, live, previously-undiscovered production issue found
-- during a full re-detection pass: Stratxcel's OWN Google OAuth (GA4,
-- Search Console, Gmail, Calendar) is broken for the real, actively-used
-- platform tenant, while a near-empty duplicate tenant happens to have a
-- working connection. Applied live via Supabase MCP on 2026-09-02; this
-- file makes it reproducible from a fresh database.

insert into public.capability_registry
  (capability_key, name, description, category, skill, agent_tool_name, package_or_module, department, connection, required_permission, read_write, tenant_scope, cost_profile, risk, verification_method, status, status_notes, external_blocker, last_verified_at, last_verified_by)
values
  ('capability:stratxcel_own_google_oauth_expired', 'Stratxcel''s OWN Google OAuth (GA4/Search Console/Gmail/Calendar) is genuinely broken in production right now -- confirmed via a full re-detection pass', 'Found during a full re-detection pass (2026-09-02, later same day) that re-verified every named connection against live database state rather than trusting prior status reports. search_google_connections for tenant 872723d5-0c21-4638-8921-99213c4ed63a -- confirmed via crm_leads (1 row)/missions (72 rows)/search_projects (1 row) to be the real, actively-used Stratxcel platform tenant, not a duplicate -- shows status=''error'', last_error=''Google token refresh failed: HTTP 400'', last successful sync 2026-08-09, not updated since 2026-08-20. owner_sources shows the same real, live symptom as of TODAY (last_sync_at 2026-09-02 07:35 UTC): gmail and google_calendar both status=ERROR with the identical last_error (''Google token refresh failed: HTTP 400''), gmail''s last real success 2026-08-17. HTTP 400 on a token refresh call is Google''s standard invalid_grant response -- the refresh token has been revoked or expired and cannot self-heal; this requires the owner to manually re-authenticate via a real OAuth consent flow, which this agent cannot do on its own. A SEPARATE, mostly-unused duplicate tenant (466e6195-a9f6-4576-8271-29fdae61c18a -- 1 search_projects row, ZERO crm_leads/missions/workforce_plans) happens to have a currently-connected, recently-synced (2026-09-01) Google connection for the same GA4 property (538010450) and the same search_console_site_url -- someone apparently completed a fresh Google OAuth connect under the WRONG (near-empty) tenant at some point, leaving the real, actively-used tenant''s connection broken. Real, concrete production impact: every tool this session built that reads real GA4/Search Console data for Stratxcel''s own tenant by default (check_growth_status, run_growth_analysis, check_plan_outcomes, revise_growth_plan) has been operating against STALE data for the real Stratxcel tenant since ~2026-08-09/20 -- new search_measurement_snapshots have not been captured since then for that tenant. Google Drive (owner_sources) shows status=CONNECTED but last_sync_at is null -- never actually verified by a real sync attempt, so its true health is unconfirmed despite the CONNECTED label.', 'ecosystem', null, null, 'search_google_connections; owner_sources', 'Engineering', 'google', null, 'read', 'tenant', 'free', 'read', 'Live queries against search_google_connections and owner_sources for both real Stratxcel tenant rows, cross-referenced against crm_leads/missions/search_projects/workforce_plans row counts to confirm which tenant is genuinely in active use (872723d5..., 72 real missions) versus which is a near-empty duplicate (466e6195..., 0 missions) that happens to hold the currently-working Google connection.', 'EXTERNAL_REQUIRED', 'Two real remediation options, neither of which this agent can perform unilaterally: (1) the account owner re-authenticates Google OAuth for the real tenant (872723d5...) via the existing, already-built connect flow, which would generate a fresh refresh token and restore GA4/Search Console/Gmail/Calendar sync; or (2) if the working connection under the near-empty duplicate tenant (466e6195...) was itself a deliberate, correct reconnection, the two tenants'' data should be consolidated onto one canonical tenant id -- a real, deliberate data-migration decision requiring explicit owner approval, not something to do silently.', 'google_oauth_refresh_token_invalid_requires_owner_reauthentication', now(), 'claude_session_2026-09-02')
on conflict (capability_key) do nothing;
